## 55. Solved Example 5 — Hidden Opposite Corner

Suppose a corner contains:

```text
1, 2, 3
```

and:

```text
1 ↔ 6
2 ↔ 5
3 ↔ 4
```

Then the diagonally opposite corner contains:

```text
6, 5, 4
```

#### Answer

```text
(6, 5, 4)
```

---

## 56. Solved Example 6 — One Common Edge

Suppose:

```text
View A = 1, 2, 3
View B = 1, 2, 5
```

The common edge is:

```text
1—2
```

The two other faces are:

```text
3 and 5
```

Under the appropriate same-edge orientation, these lie on opposite sides, so:

```text
3 ↔ 5
```

This is one of the most useful advanced patterns.

---

## 57. Solved Example 7 — Four Neighbours

Suppose the following combinations are known:

```text
(1,2,3)
(1,3,4)
(1,4,5)
```

Then 1 is adjacent to:

```text
2,3,4,5
```

So the remaining face 6 is opposite 1.

---

## 58. Solved Example 8 — Symbolic Die

Views:

```text
(★, ●, ▲)
(★, ■, ●)
(★, ◆, ■)
```

For `★`:

```text
Adjacent = ●, ▲, ■, ◆
```

The only remaining symbol:

```text
♥
```

must be opposite ★.

Therefore:

```text
★ ↔ ♥
```

---

## 59. Solved Example 9 — Rolling

Initial position:

```text
TOP = 1
FRONT = 2
RIGHT = 3
```

Roll forward once.

The cycle is:

```text
TOP → FRONT
FRONT → BOTTOM
BOTTOM → BACK
BACK → TOP
```

Therefore the new top becomes the old back.

If:

```text
BACK = 5
```

then:

```text
NEW TOP = 5
```

---

## 60. Solved Example 10 — Two Rolls

Initial:

```text
TOP = 1
FRONT = 2
BOTTOM = 6
BACK = 5
```

Roll forward twice.

First roll:

```text
TOP = 5
FRONT = 1
BOTTOM = 2
BACK = 6
```

Second roll:

```text
TOP = 6
FRONT = 5
BOTTOM = 1
BACK = 2
```

Therefore after 180°:

```text
TOP = 6
```

---

## 61. Fast Method for Exam Options

When four options are given:

### Step 1

Check opposite pairs.

```text
If an option places opposites together
→ reject immediately.
```

### Step 2

Check corner compatibility.

```text
A valid corner cannot contain an opposite pair.
```

### Step 3

Check adjacency.

```text
Every pair shown on connected edges must be adjacent.
```

### Step 4

Only then perform detailed rotation/orientation analysis.

This saves time.

---

## 62. Elimination Flowchart

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Start Dice Problem] --> B[Identify labels]
    B --> C[Find known opposite pairs]
    C --> D{Any opposite pair touching?}
    D -- Yes --> E[Reject option]
    D -- No --> F{Need exact orientation?}
    F -- No --> G[Answer by adjacency/opposite rule]
    F -- Yes --> H[Choose reference corner]
    H --> I[Track cube rotation]
    I --> J{Orientation matches?}
    J -- Yes --> K[Valid]
    J -- No --> E
```

---

## 63. Decision Tree

```text
                 START
                   |
          ┌────────┴────────┐
          |                 |
   Opposite pairs known?   NO
          |                 |
         YES            collect views
          |
   Check touching faces
          |
    ┌─────┴─────┐
    |           |
 contradiction  valid
    |           |
  reject     need rotation?
                |
          ┌─────┴─────┐
          |           |
         NO          YES
          |           |
       answer    track orientation
```

